Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"3dd58979-83cc-6c4a-93e1-ca34a6facce0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"64d11888-ffca-d546-b155-187e317b0326"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"4d24dd97-cf92-a247-bcab-ce62b99278b9"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"db927dc8-6368-a74b-9e6f-9473960035fc"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"57564e78-c1e4-944d-9bdc-a0ea91b4d686"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b477e0fe-8b6e-564a-b088-15992f9f44dd"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"01e95776-6adc-474f-8311-d76ca252ca88"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"65960b3e-4dc7-7c4f-998f-9f50c309c307"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"c29a273c-b091-5648-80ec-2e13daea1da9"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7659d3d2-4c8d-6147-a79b-74e31ab5ed7e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"735e850e-4030-0d4c-b6ad-10c0e48870f3"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"23cb3644-89ae-284d-bed7-5a2389c51281"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"53e64f43-8daf-b147-b47c-6a7c6b5c4ff3"],

